## §1 Variable namespace

### Field ownership summary

Every combat variable belongs to exactly one of five owners. The owner
determines its scope, lifetime, and whether reads/writes outside the
designated window are valid. The detailed tables below this row group
fields by *category* (core state, per-slot stats, etc.); this row
groups them by *owner* for the "where does this live?" lookup.

| Owner | Scope it lives on | Lifetime | Variables |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Host** | combat host (PC) character | combat init → combat cleanup | `pod_combat_active`, `pod_combat_is_over`, `pod_combat_round`, `pod_combat_current_actor_team`, `pod_combat_current_actor_position`, `pod_combat_current_ap`, `pod_combat_player_team_size`, `pod_combat_enemy_team_size`, `pod_combat_pc_target_team`, `pod_combat_pc_target_position`, `pod_combat_pc_target_char`, `pod_combat_selected_target_team`, `pod_combat_selected_target_position`, `pod_combat_pc_slot` / `pod_combat_enemy_leader_slot` (the only two literal slot-pointer vars — the player/0 and enemy/0 team leaders), `pod_combat_active_slots` (variable list of every filled slot story, lazily populated as slots fill; every non-leader slot is reached by iterating it and matching `combat_team` + `team_position`), `pod_combat_winner`, `pod_combat_loser`, `pod_combat_last_damage`, `pod_combat_last_heal_amount`, `pod_combat_last_morale_damage_amount`, `pod_combat_last_morale_heal_amount`, `pod_combat_last_outcome`, `pod_combat_last_attack_result`, `pod_combat_last_retal_fired`, `pod_combat_last_retal_damage`, `pod_combat_last_retal_agg`, `pod_combat_nonfatal_active` |
| **Slot** | `POD_combat_slot` story (one per slot, on Charon) | slot creation → slot cleanup | `combat_team`, `team_position`, `slot_char`, `slot_alive`, `slot_morale`, `slot_prowess`, `slot_soak`, `slot_base_soak`, `slot_hit_chance`, `slot_base_hit_chance`, `slot_initiative`, `slot_init_bonus`, `slot_ap_drain`, `slot_energy_used`, `slot_turn_order`, `slot_has_acted`, `slot_is_guarding`, `slot_is_dodging`, `slot_is_stealthed`, `slot_retaliate_*`, `slot_incorporeal_spirit`, `slot_can_damage_spirit`, all `slot_{stat}_{direction}_{duration}_tier` vars |
| **Workspace (transient)** | combat host | **only between `pod_combat_load_workspace_effect` and `pod_combat_save_workspace_effect`** | `pod_combat_actor_*`, `pod_combat_target_*`, `pod_combat_current_hit_chance` (mirrors of the slot fields above) |
| **Character (AI)** | the acting AI character | persists per-character across combats until `pod_combat_group_cleanup_effect` clears them | `pod_combat_ai_last_move`, `pod_combat_ai_prev_move`, `pod_combat_ai_prev2_move`, `pod_combat_loadout` (variable list) |
| **Log entry** | `POD_combat_log_entry` story (one per log row, on Charon) | combat init → combat cleanup (all entries end together) | `entry.var:outcome`, `entry.var:attack_result`, `entry.var:retal_fired` (three-axis result snapshot — see §4), `entry.var:damage`, `entry.var:heal_amount`, `entry.var:morale_damage_amount`, `entry.var:morale_heal_amount`, `entry.var:retal_damage`, `entry.var:retal_agg`, `entry.var:actor_side` (team code of the acting slot — `0` ally/player / `1` enemy / `-1` system entry; the combat-log GUI keys the ally-gold / enemy-red side bar + actor-name tint off this), `entry.var:self_damage` (post-soak recoil, set only when > 0), `entry.var:aoe_burst_index` (set by AoE iterations so intent segments and the recoil segment render once per move; absent on non-AoE rows), `entry.var:system_message` (only on bookend rows pushed by `pod_combat_push_system_log_effect`), `entry.var:round`, plus the move-context fields the customizable_loc dispatcher reads |

HP is derived live from each slot character's PoD wound vars
(`POD_empty_damage_boxes` etc.); it is **not** owned by any of the
above.

The workspace row is the only one with a sub-action lifetime. The
*Action workspace lifecycle invariant* in §7 spells out the load/save
contract that gives those vars meaning.

### Core state (on the combat host / PC character)

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `pod_combat_active` | flag: combat is in progress |
| `pod_combat_is_over` | flag: combat is over (re-entry guard) |
| `pod_combat_round` | current round number |
| `pod_combat_current_actor_team` / `_position` | the acting combatant's team (`flag:player` / `flag:enemy`) + position within it (int 0+, 0 = leader) |
| `pod_combat_current_ap` | AP remaining this turn |
| `pod_combat_player_team_size` | count of occupied player positions; incremented as each ally is seated by `POD_combat_duel_add_ally_effect` (uncapped — soft guardrail `pod_combat_max_team_size` only) |
| `pod_combat_enemy_team_size` | count of occupied enemy positions; incremented as each enemy is seated by `POD_combat_duel_add_enemy_effect` (uncapped — soft guardrail `pod_combat_max_team_size` only) |
| `pod_combat_pc_target_team` / `_position` | the PC's persistent target: team + position (never the PC's own player/0) |
| `pod_combat_selected_target_team` / `_position` | the slot (team + position) loaded into the target workspace |
| `pod_combat_pc_slot` / `pod_combat_enemy_leader_slot` | the only two literal slot-pointer vars: the player/0 and enemy/0 team leaders. Each resolves to that leader's `POD_combat_slot` story scope. Non-leader slots have no pointer var — they are found by iterating `pod_combat_active_slots`. |
| `pod_combat_active_slots` | variable list of slot stories currently in play (filled slots only, in insertion order: player leader then any allies, then enemy leader then the rest). Iterated by every dispatch loop (matching `combat_team` + `team_position` for a specific slot) so the dispatchers scale to any team size with no unrolling. |

### Per-slot stats (vars on each `POD_combat_slot` story)

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `combat_team` | flag (`flag:player` / `flag:enemy`): the slot's team, baked at creation |
| `team_position` | int 0+: position within the team (0 = leader), no upper bound, baked at creation |
| `slot_char` | character ref occupying the slot |
| `slot_alive` | 1 while in play, 0 when KO'd |
| `slot_morale` | current Morale |
| `slot_prowess` | current prowess |
| `slot_soak` | live soak chance (0-100) |
| `slot_base_soak` | soak before any tier effects |
| `slot_hit_chance` | live hit chance (20-95) |
| `slot_base_hit_chance` | hit chance before any tier effects |
| `slot_initiative` | initiative roll this round |
| `slot_init_bonus` | next-round initiative modifier |
| `slot_ap_drain` | pending AP drain: consumed (floor 0) at the victim's next turn start, then cleared. Writes are take-max. A drain >= base AP (`ap_drain_6`) is the stun — 0 AP means no affordable move, so the turn is lost. Drives the dazed status icon + dazed/stunned log rows |
| `slot_energy_used` | counter for AI energy-attrition weighting |
| `slot_turn_order` | turn-rank within the round (1 = first); stamped by `pod_combat_calc_turn_orders_effect` after initiative roll |
| `slot_has_acted` | 1 once the slot's turn resolves this round; reset to 0 by `pod_combat_calculate_initiative_effect` at the start of every round |
| `slot_dot_amount` / `slot_dot_rounds` | active burn (DoT): damage per round-end tick / rounds remaining. Absence = no burn (the tick loop filters on `has_variable = slot_dot_rounds`); re-application overwrites |
| `slot_dot_kind` | LITERAL flag typing the burn: `flag:morale`, a damage source (`flag:fire` etc.), or `flag:duel` for untyped. Always set while a burn is active — status icon, log dispatch, and wound dispatch all read it |
| `slot_dot_aggravated` | 0/1, always set with the burn: when 1, untyped ticks route as `duel_aggravated` (mirrors the move's `damage_type = aggravated`); ignored for typed sources (PoD's classifier types those per victim splat) |

Team affiliation is stored explicitly on each slot as the `combat_team`
flag (`flag:player` / `flag:enemy`); `team_position` (int 0+, 0 = leader)
gives the position within that team. There is no flat slot index.

**Health is NOT stored on the slot story.** Live script values
derive HP from each slot character's PoD wound vars. The slot
story only holds the `slot_char` pointer; the SVs read
`POD_empty_damage_boxes` / `POD_total_damage_boxes` /
`POD_health_aggravated_damage_num` off the character:

| SV | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `pod_combat_slot_hp_value` | empty wound boxes (HP remaining) |
| `pod_combat_slot_max_hp_value` | wound track length (max HP) |
| `pod_combat_slot_agg_damage_sv` | aggravated wound boxes |
| `pod_combat_slot_total_damage_sv` | total wound boxes filled |


### Per-slot stance flags (on the `POD_combat_slot` story)

All persist across rounds; only cleared when consumed or at combat end.

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `slot_is_guarding` | Guard stance active |
| `slot_is_dodging` | Dodge stance active |
| `slot_is_stealthed` | Stealth active (includes +30 hit) |
| `slot_retaliate_hit` | retaliation damage if hit |
| `slot_retaliate_miss` | retaliation damage if missed |
| `slot_retaliate_{hit,miss}_agg` | aggravated variants |

### Per-slot spirit-damage capability

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `slot_incorporeal_spirit` | slot character is incorporeal; physical attacks no-op unless the attacker has `slot_can_damage_spirit` |
| `slot_can_damage_spirit` | slot character can land physical hits on incorporeal targets |

### Tier variables (on the `POD_combat_slot` story)

Tier = 1 (small, ±10), 2 (medium, ±20), 3 (large, ±30). Live stats
are rebuilt from base + sum of active tier magnitudes. See the
**Tier system** section below.

```
slot_{stat}_{direction}_{duration}_tier
  stat:      soak | hit
  direction: buff | debuff
  duration:  round (cleared at round end) | combat (lasts the fight)
```

### Action workspace (transient — acting combatant + current target)

Mirrors the per-slot fields for whoever is currently acting / targeted.
Lives on the combat host so saved scopes / scripted-effect parameters
can read it without crossing into the slot-story scope.

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `pod_combat_actor_*` | actor's stats (loaded from `current_actor` slot) |
| `pod_combat_target_*` | target's stats (loaded from `selected_target` slot) |
| `pod_combat_current_hit_chance` | active attacker's hit chance this attack |

Most tier, stance, retaliation, spirit, and `base_*` fields exist on
both sides — load/save effects walk slot stories and write into /
read back from the matching workspace mirror. As of the workspace-mirror
symmetrization, the mirrors are **fully symmetric**: every field —
including `slot_init_bonus`, `slot_ap_drain`, and `slot_energy_used` — is
loaded and saved on BOTH the actor and target side. Both sides flow
through one parametric pair, `pod_combat_load_side_from_story_helper` /
`pod_combat_save_side_to_story_helper` (`SIDE = actor|target`); the four
public load/save effects (`load_actor` / `load_target` / `save_actor` /
`save_target`) are thin wrappers over them.

A few fields only have a live reader on one side (e.g. `slot_energy_used`
feeds the actor-side AI energy-attrition weighting; the target-side
mirror is no-op overhead), but they're mirrored anyway for shape
uniformity — one helper body, no per-field branching.

When you add a new slot field, mirror it on both sides (one line in each
helper). See §11 *Adding a new workspace mirror field*.

**Lifecycle contract:** These variables are valid ONLY between a
`pod_combat_load_workspace_effect` call and the matching
`pod_combat_save_workspace_effect`. Any other code path that reads
them is reading stale data — canonical per-combatant state lives on
the slot story. See §7 *Action workspace lifecycle invariant* for
the full statement and enforcement strategy.

### Result / display

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `pod_combat_winner` | character ref: who won (or team leader) |
| `pod_combat_loser` | character ref: who lost |
| `pod_combat_last_damage` | last HP damage amount dealt |
| `pod_combat_last_heal_amount` | last HP heal amount applied |
| `pod_combat_last_morale_damage_amount` | last morale damage amount |
| `pod_combat_last_morale_heal_amount` | last morale heal amount |
| `pod_combat_last_retal_damage` | last retaliation damage amount |
| `pod_combat_last_outcome` | top-level outcome flag (`flag:attack` / `heal` / `morale_damage` / `morale_healed` / `utility`) — see §4 |
| `pod_combat_last_attack_result` | inner attack resolution (`flag:hp_damage` / `soaked` / `missed` / `dodged` / `stealthed` / `guard_blocked`); only meaningful when outcome=attack |
| `pod_combat_last_retal_fired` | overlay flag — 1 when retaliation fired on this row, absent otherwise |

The move story is no longer host-side; `push_log` receives it as an
explicit `MOVE_STORY` parameter from `POD_execute_combat_move §16`.

### AI move-history (per-actor, NOT per-host)

These live on the acting AI character object — written directly by
`pod_combat_ai_select_and_execute_move_effect` immediately after each
pick (a 3-deep ring shift: prev2 ← prev, prev ← last, last ← chosen).
Cleared during the AI-side branch of `pod_combat_group_cleanup_effect`
at combat end, alongside the per-AI `pod_combat_loadout` list. They are
STORY REFERENCES (point at a `POD_combat_move` scope), not flags. The
AI selector uses `this = scope:ai_actor.var:pod_combat_ai_last_move`
style scope-equality checks for anti-repetition penalties — see the
`@ai_repeat_last / prev / prev2` tuning constants in
`pod_combat_ai_effects.txt`.

| Variable | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `pod_combat_ai_last_move` | story ref: most recent move |
| `pod_combat_ai_prev_move` | story ref: 2 turns ago |
| `pod_combat_ai_prev2_move` | story ref: 3 turns ago |

